pub const PROMPT_VERSION: u32 = 9;

pub const SVG_PROMPT: &str = "Reconstruct the attached application icon as one clean 1024 by 1024 SVG. Preserve its exact recognizable identity, silhouette, proportions, logo geometry, typography converted to paths, and meaningful details. Use one full-canvas opaque <g id=\"background\"> followed by one to four material groups <g id=\"group-1\"> through <g id=\"group-4\"> in back-to-front z order. Every material group must contain one to four independent child groups named <g id=\"layer-G-L\">, where G is the material-group number and L is the child-layer number. Keep elements that should move as one glass object in the same group; put independently separated shapes in different child layers or groups. A single wordmark, line of text, or adjacent logo lockup must stay co-planar: place all of its paths in one group with data-liquid-mode=\"combined\" and never split its glyphs or neighboring pieces across different z groups. Treat a full-bleed color field as the background itself: do not represent it as a full-canvas circle, rounded square, or other pre-defined canvas mask in a foreground group; the renderer supplies the final rounded-rectangle mask. Preserve circles and other shapes when they are meaningful logo artwork rather than a full-bleed backdrop. Represent negative space inside an artwork silhouette, such as eyes, holes and apertures, as transparent cutouts in the underlying foreground path (use compound paths and fill-rule when needed); never paint those cutouts with the current background colour or put them in a separate opaque layer. Keep the original icon optically centered and at its recognizable scale on the 1024 grid; never invent a new badge, scene, mockup, border, or padding. Keep artwork flat and vector-only. Do not embed raster images, external resources, scripts, text/font elements, filters, blur, shadows, glow, bevel, refraction, masks, rounded-square canvas masks, mockups, UI screenshots, or invented symbols. Return only the JSON object required by the output schema.";
